  "notes": [
    "Coordinates are the approximate location of the provincial administrative centre (the ward/city where the provincial People's Committee sits after 1/7/2025, per the trung tâm chính trị - hành chính list attached to Nghị quyết 60-NQ/TW and the ward names on Wikipedia \"Provinces of Vietnam\"; coordinates from OpenStreetMap Nominatim / Wikipedia), rounded to 4 decimals; for weather only.",
    "Seat names are the familiar pre-2025 city names (Quy Nhơn, Đồng Hới, Tân An, …). City- and district-level units were abolished on 1/7/2025, so the centre now lies in a ward (e.g. phường Quy Nhơn, phường Đồng Hới, phường Long An); weather apps should treat the seat as a place label, not an administrative unit.",
    "Hải Phòng: most city departments moved to the new political-administrative centre north of the Cấm river (phường Thủy Nguyên); the point used is central Hải Phòng, about 2 km away, which makes no difference for weather.",
    "Region assignment: bac = Northwest, Northeast and Red River Delta (15 units); trung = Thanh Hóa through Lâm Đồng, i.e. North Central, South Central Coast and Central Highlands (11 units); nam = Southeast and Mekong Delta (8 units). Borderline cases follow the merged unit's administrative centre and its pre-2025 region: Lâm Đồng (+ Đắk Nông, Bình Thuận; centre Đà Lạt, Central Highlands) = trung; Gia Lai (+ Bình Định; centre Quy Nhơn) = trung; Đắk Lắk (+ Phú Yên; centre Buôn Ma Thuột) = trung; Quảng Ngãi (+ Kon Tum) = trung; Khánh Hòa (+ Ninh Thuận) = trung; Đồng Nai (+ Bình Phước, both Southeast) = nam; Tây Ninh (+ Long An; centre Tân An) = nam.",
    "Weather caveat: one point per unit. Some merged units span very different climates from their centre — Lâm Đồng (Đà Lạt highland vs. coastal former Bình Thuận/Phan Thiết), Gia Lai (coastal Quy Nhơn vs. highland Pleiku), Đắk Lắk (Buôn Ma Thuột vs. coastal Tuy Hòa), Quảng Ngãi (coast vs. Kon Tum), Lào Cai (Yên Bái vs. Sa Pa).",
    "formerly lists all pre-2025 provincial units merged into the new unit (including the one whose name was kept); [] means not reorganised. 11 unchanged + 52 merged = 63 former units. Names, seats and formerly use the official modern tone placement of the Nghị quyết texts (Khánh Hòa, Thanh Hóa, Hòa Bình, Biên Hòa); the old style (Khánh Hoà, Thanh Hoá) is in aka where it is the unit's own name. Search should fold diacritics and tone placement.",
    "kind reflects the 1/7/2025 structure (6 thành phố + 28 tỉnh). Later changes are recorded in laterChanges: Đồng Nai became a centrally-run city on 30/4/2026, Quảng Ninh on 1/9/2026 and Bắc Ninh on 20/9/2026 (9 thành phố + 25 tỉnh from 20/9/2026). Names and boundaries did not change. Each laterChanges entry links the official full text in source.",
    "sources: the official full texts first (Báo Chính phủ for Nghị quyết 202/2025/QH15; Cổng TTĐT Chính phủ — Xây dựng chính sách, pháp luật for Nghị quyết 30, 36 and 39/2026/QH16), then the reference lists and coordinate sources; the news reports at the end are secondary."
  ],
